Variation of different variables (Q, $C, V, E$ and $U$ ) of parallel plate capacitor when dielectric $(K)$ is introduced when battery is removed is \begin{array}{ll}
C^{\prime}=K C & E^{\prime}=E / K \\
Q^{\prime}=Q & U^{\prime}=U / K \\
V^{\prime}=V / K &
\end{array}

$\begin{aligned}& V_{\text{comma }}=\frac{C_1 V_1+C_2 V_2}{C_1+C_2}\left(\because V_2=0\right) \\
& \Rightarrow V_{\text{comma }}=\frac{C_1 V_1}{C_1+C_2}
\end{aligned}$

Here $C_1, C_2 and C_3$ are in series.
 $\frac{1}{C^{\prime}}=\frac{1}{C}+\frac{1}{2 C}+\frac{1}{3 C} \begin{aligned}
\frac{1}{C^{\prime}}& =\frac{6+3+2}{6 C}=\frac{11}{6 C}\\
\Rightarrow \quad C & =\frac{6 C}{11}
\end{aligned}All the $capacitors in branch number 1 is in series so the charge on each number capacitor is: Q^{\prime}=$\frac{6}{11}$ C V Also charge on capacitor $C_4$ is $Q=4$ V \therefore $\text{ Ratio }=\frac{Q^{\prime}}{Q}=\frac{6 \mathrm{CV}}{11 \times 4 C V}=\frac{3}{22}$
